/*!
@defgroup mbc MBC: Memory Block Checker Driver
@details The MCUXpresso SDK provides a driver for the Memory Block Checker (MBC)
submodule of the Trusted Resource Domain Controller (TRDC).

The MBC hardware allows software to configure per-block access policies for
slave memories for DSC platforms. Each block can independently permit or deny read, write, and
execute access for the primary bus master and the secondary bus master.

@{

# MBC functions {#MBCFunc}

The MBC driver provides the following functionality:
 - Query hardware configuration: TRDC_GetMbcHardwareConfig().
 - Configure memory access control policies: TRDC_MbcSetMemoryAccessConfig().
 - Configure individual memory block access: TRDC_MbcSetMemoryBlockConfig().
 - Clear access violation errors: TRDC_MbcClearError().

# Typical use case {#MBCTypical}

## Configure and test a MBC memory block {#MBCConfig}

Refer to the driver example code located at
<em>examples/driver_examples/dsc_mbc/basic/mbc.c</em>.

*/
/*! @} */
